    "body": "### Problem\n\n  With autocomplete enabled and `complete=o,b`, buffer candidates show source paths until the LSP response arrives. The paths then disappear.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n  ```lua\nvim.o.autocomplete = true\nvim.o.complete = 'o,b'\n```\nWith another listed buffer containing a matching word, type its prefix in an LSP-attached buffer and observe the candidate’s source path disappear when LSP results arrive.\n\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThe LSP refresh preserves buffer candidates’ source paths.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.12.3; also reproduced at commit 3068a8f652\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nn/a\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nmacOS 26.6.2\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nalacritty\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nalacritty\n\n### Installation\n\nbuild from repo",
